# What comes out of the dark.
#
# There are no turns here, so there are no `move` blocks, no patterns, no phases and no intents:
# an enemy's whole behaviour is its own `on every <n>s:` listeners, pumped by the clock. Writing
# one of the turn-shaped ones under `clock ticks` is error CT337, and its message says what the
# real-time shape of the same idea is. That is the single largest difference between writing a
# real-time enemy and a turn-based one, and FINDINGS #2 and #3 are about what it costs.
#
# None of them places itself: whoever spawns a wave chooses where it walks in, because a lane is
# a decision above the fight. `runtime.Place(who, lane, rank)` is that call from C#, and the
# `arrive` verb in places.cantrip is the same move in the game's own words, for the tests. A
# spawn does raise `created` now, so content can meet an arrival -- an effect, a relic that hears
# anything entering the fight -- which nothing could before. FINDINGS #5.
#
# `random party` rather than `player`: `player` is the leader alone, and an enemy that always
# swings at the leader is the bug CT326 exists to stop. CT326 reads a listener now, so writing
# `deal 5 to player` on any line below is refused at lint. FINDINGS #3a.

# The common one. Closes a rank every two seconds; once it is on the line it swings instead.
enemy "Hollow"
  hp 16
  on every 2s:
    if not self.has(Reeling):
      if self.rank > 0:
        self.rank -1
      else:
        deal 5 to random party

# Never closes. Stands where it arrived and throws, which is what makes `range` matter: a keeper
# who spends everything on what is nearest never reaches the Wisps and loses slowly.
enemy "Wisp"
  hp 10
  on every 3s:
    deal 3 to random party

# Slow and heavy, and angrier once it is hurt. A phase gates a `move`, and there are no moves
# here, so the halfway change is a filter on a second listener instead.
enemy "Breaker"
  hp 40
  on every 3s:
    if self.rank > 0:
      self.rank -1
    else:
      deal 9 to random party
  on every 3s (self.hp <= self.max_hp / 2):
    deal 4 to random party
